      "{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\n\\n## Message\\nDo toggles persist?\\n\\n## Response protocol (advice phase, trigger: user-message)\\nNothing to add is the expected answer, and the most common one. Then respond with exactly NO_COMMENT and nothing else: no JSON, no explanation, no punctuation. It adds nothing to the thread. Here it means the moment touches nothing in your domain, whatever it says to build or not to use.\\nOnly when it touches something your domain says already exists, respond with JSON only, exactly this shape: { \\\"snippets\\\": string[], \\\"layers\\\": string[], \\\"confidence\\\": number }.\\n\\\"snippets\\\" are the remarks of your pointer, one per line of the charter's shape, in its order; \\\"layers\\\" are IDs of your domain's layers to inject; at least one of them is non-empty. \\\"confidence\\\" is a number from 0 to 1.\\nAny other answer, including JSON with empty lists or extra fields, is an error, not a comment.\"}]},\"uuid\":\"01a1f234-191f-743a-b0e6-0aef7df7bf1f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null}"
